/**
 * @defgroup compressed_air_desktop_migration_boundaries Desktop Migration Boundaries
 * @ingroup compressor_modeling
 * @brief Boundary between Suite compressor assessment kernels and AMO-Tools-Desktop adapters.
 * @details Suite now owns reusable compressed-air assessment calculations that require
 *          algorithm documentation: compressor performance-point generation, compressor
 *          profile rows, multi-compressor allocation, profile savings rollups, and scalar
 *          EEM transforms. Desktop remains the application layer.
 *
 * @heading{Suite Responsibilities}
 * Suite functions operate on already-normalized U.S. customary inputs and return passive
 * result objects or registered vectors:
 * - `generatePerformancePoints` returns default compressor points.
 * - `calculateBaselineProfile` returns interval compressor rows from profile input data.
 * - `reallocateProfileFlow` distributes system demand across available compressors.
 * - `calculateProfileTotals` returns total system interval demand and power.
 * - `calculateProfileSavings` returns annual energy, cost, savings, and simple payback.
 * - EEM helpers return reusable airflow, pressure, receiver, and set-point transforms.
 *
 * @heading{Desktop Responsibilities}
 * Desktop should continue to own metric conversion, UI validation, display flags, assessment
 * persistence, report shaping, modification labels, notes, modal state, CO2 service integration,
 * and mapping Desktop numeric IDs to Suite enums. Desktop may keep calculations that are
 * exclusively presentation, ordering, or form-state logic.
 *
 * @heading{Units}
 * Suite compressor assessment APIs use package power @unitb{\kilo\watt}, airflow
 * @unitb{\acfm}, pressure @unitb{\psig} or @unitb{\psia}, receiver volume @unitb{\cubicFoot},
 * time @unitb{\hour} or @unitb{\second}, electricity @unitb{\kilo\watt\hour}, and cost
 * @unitb{\dollar}. Fractions are @unitb{\unitless}; percentages are @unitb{\percent}.
 */
